A cloud adoption readiness assessment evaluates whether an organization is prepared to move workloads to Azure. Technical infrastructure is only one part of cloud adoption; people, processes, governance, security, and finances must also be considered.

Assessment areas include:

* Business objectives
* Existing infrastructure
* Application dependencies
* Network readiness
* Identity readiness
* Security requirements
* Skills and training
* Governance
* Cost planning
* Migration strategy

For example, before migrating an on-premises application, an organization can identify its database dependencies, network requirements, authentication model, and recovery requirements.

A real-life use case is a company assessing hundreds of applications before deciding which workloads should be migrated, modernized, retained, or retired.

Readiness assessments reduce migration surprises and improve cloud adoption planning.
